  "worked_solution": "First, notice that since $x=3{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}+5{b}_{3},$ we have\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nGiven the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C,$ we find the coordinates of $x$ relative to $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}[\\,x\\,]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
